---
title: "Progress"
description: "Styled native progress element, for determinate and indeterminate states."
tags: [feedback, css]
usage: |
  Add the `progress` class to a `<progress>`. Set `value` and `max` for a known
  amount of work; leave `value` out for an indeterminate state. The text inside is
  a fallback for browsers that cannot render it.
accessibility: |
  - Always pair it with a `<label>`, so the value is announced with a name.
  - For waits of unknown length with no visible progress, consider the Spinner.
customProperties:
  "--progress-color": "Color of the filled part."
  "--progress-track": "Color of the track."
  "--progress-size": "Height of the bar."
  "--progress-radius": "Corner radius."
---

<link rel="stylesheet" href="./styles.css" media="screen">

<label for="upload">Uploading</label>
<progress id="upload" class="progress" value="65" max="100">65%</progress>

<label for="loading">Loading</label>
<progress id="loading" class="progress">Loading</progress>
